"""Skill-routed scoped AnaSOP update after the authorized first fit.
Responsibilities: data-briefing Section 3; data-preprocessing Section 4;
estimation-framework-planning Sections 5-7. Section 8 remains pending.
"""
from pathlib import Path
import re,json,sys
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2];sys.path.insert(0,str(ROOT/'src/preprocessing'))
from prepare_three_ward_unet_exact_pilot import OUT,REPORT,read,write,sha

def section(text,n):
 m=re.search(r'^## '+str(n)+r'\..*?(?=^## \d+\.|\Z)',text,re.M|re.S);return m.group(0)
def append_to(text,n,addition):
 old=section(text,n);return text.replace(old,old.rstrip()+'\n\n'+addition.strip()+'\n\n',1)
def main():
 path=ROOT/'docs/AnaSOP.md';text=path.read_text();before=text
 if '### First exact-label learning pilot' in text:raise FileExistsError('AnaSOP pilot already documented')
 (REPORT/'previous-AnaSOP.md').write_text(before)
 summary=read(REPORT/'summary.json');done=read(REPORT/'completion.json');validation=read(REPORT/'delivery_validation.json');assert validation['all_checks_passed'];mm=summary['validation_three_ward_paired_macro']
 pre=text.split('\n\n## 1.')[0]
 newpre='''# AnaSOP

Analysis Standard Operating Procedure

Design revision: 2026-10-16-r1. Current authorized scope: the first bounded conditional U-Net exact-label pilot using twelve training and four validation parent candidates, compared with always-dry and training-event retrieval baselines. This single fit is complete. Original family partitions and quality masks are preserved; normalization uses training inputs only. Sealed tests, challenge responses, additional hydraulic scenarios, additional fits, interval supervision and graph fitting remain outside this completed trial. Earlier implementation paragraphs retain the history of successive holds and qualifications; the dated first-learning notes in Sections 3-7 state the current limited release. Full-study architecture, sample-size and publication plans remain proposals. Numeric training settings are documented implementation choices within the requested pilot, not separately user-finalized research decisions.'''
 text=text.replace(pre,newpre,1)
 text=append_to(text,3,'''### First-learning data status

The first bounded learning experiment uses exactly the twelve qualified training and four qualified validation parents already described above, without new hydraulic execution or sample replacement. All sixteen inherit the original numerical event gates and exact, interval and quarantined masks. A limited trial allowlist releases only original exact-label support for the corresponding training or validation purpose; the historical default response registry remains closed. The trial stores a fixed common-grid predictor tensor, training-fitted normalization, one selected learned response per parent, and per-parent performance and coverage summaries. Validation labels are used for checkpoint selection and development evaluation, never input scaling or retrieval-candidate fitting. No main-test or challenge responses are opened. The four validation parents remain a small, reused development set; these data cannot establish observed-event accuracy, sufficient sample diversity or independent held-out performance.''')
 text=text.replace('Final-variable status remains `no` until the research reference, input encoding and label-admission policy are frozen for a new event library; technical construction does not authorize training or certify physical accuracy.','Final-variable status remains `no` for the final study. A separately authorized limited first-learning interface is now frozen and described below; it does not certify physical accuracy or authorize the remaining model comparisons.',1)
 text=text.replace('Input and loader preparation tested; no network inference or training runtime measured in this task.','First-trial training elapsed time and warm prepared-feature forward time are recorded separately. Full feature assembly, loading and transfer remain outside the measured forward time; no end-to-end speedup is established.',1)
 text=append_to(text,4,'''### First-learning input encoding and scoped admission

Ground Elevation, Ground Area, Building Occupancy, Road Connectivity and Surface Parameters retain the twenty-eight existing static channels. Add the prescribed low River Stage averaged over boundary points in the same common cell, with a separate known-value indicator. Twenty-nine normalized known-value channels and their twenty-nine feature-valid indicators form fifty-eight input channels. Fit static moments on known values of the fixed geography present in the training instances, counted once rather than twelve identical copies. Unknown values are encoded as zero after normalization with validity zero; this does not declare unknown terrain to be zero elevation. Response-dependent quality masks are label-side only.

Encode Rainfall Rate and the seven prescribed River Stage increments using exact piecewise-linear integration within each of 240 one-minute bins. This produces 1,920 conditioning values over the four-hour horizon. Native second-level knots, source curves, roof redistribution, lineage and partitions are unchanged. The encoding preserves the original curve integrals but compresses sub-minute shape. Fit one mean and population standard deviation per forcing channel using training-event bins only. Constant channels use unit scale; no target normalization or validation-fitted clipping is applied. Initial Water State remains fixed dry in the interior, with no action and fixed Surface Parameters; the original roof redistribution remains represented by the static effective rainfall weight.

Exact-only supervision and primary evaluation retain the original finite coincident-bound support and all original quarantines. No bounded, unknown or excluded target is replaced by a regression zero or midpoint. Numerical placeholders outside the exact loss mask receive zero weight and zero loss gradient. The retrieval baseline returns only its selected training parent's exact targets and abstains elsewhere. The primary paired evaluation intersects the target exact mask, selected source exact mask and eligible Ground Area; all three methods use that same support. Report each method's own available exact support separately and retain all original interval and quarantine areas in the support audit. This is a scoped trial release rather than a change to the historical policy or a general release of other responses.''')
 text=append_to(text,5,'''### First-learning comparison scope

The user-authorized first trial freezes twelve original training families and four original validation families. Exactly one conditional U-Net fit is compared with always-dry and one-nearest-training-event retrieval. Nearest matching uses normalized complete Rainfall Rate curves and River Stage increment curves with equal modality weights; the seven coherent stage channels share the water-level weight. The candidate response pool contains training parents only. Training diagnostics exclude the query's own family, whereas all validation queries may use the twelve training parents. Selection never uses the target response.

The validation set selects a checkpoint and supplies development scores, so it is not an independent test. Pixels, epochs and the single initialization do not increase parent-event counts. Compare all methods on identical paired exact support, then show their full available exact coverage and abstention. This trial evaluates emulation of Peak Mean Depth only; road length, dynamic paths, river hydraulics, observational accuracy and active-measure effects remain outside its evidence. Preserve the full-study sealed evaluation and later controlled model comparisons as pending, regardless of the trial's outcome.''')
 text=text.replace('Network width, depth, forcing encoder, patch size and optimizer remain to be fixed using training and validation only. Tiled inference requires a predeclared overlap/halo and whole-domain seam assessment.','The full-study model recipe remains to be finalized using development evidence. The first-learning recipe below uses a single full-domain input rather than tiles. Any later tiled variant requires a predeclared overlap/halo and whole-domain seam assessment.',1)
 text=append_to(text,6,r'''### First exact-label learning pilot

Use a four-level conditional U-Net with widths 8, 16, 32, 64 and 128, group normalization, bilinear upsampling, feature-wise conditioning from the prescribed forcing encoding, and a nonnegative depth output. The single initialization has 671,513 learned parameters. Predict Peak Mean Depth in metres on the original full common grid; pad computational edges only and crop back before loss and evaluation. There is no spatial augmentation, patch-level partition, learned interval supervision or graph fit.

For each parent event, minimize the Ground Area weighted squared error over its original exact-label cells:

\[
L_e = \frac{\sum_{c \in E_e} A_c (\widehat{H}^{\max}_{e,c}-H^{\max}_{e,c})^2}{\sum_{c \in E_e} A_c}.
\]

Here \(e\) denotes a training parent, \(c\) a common cell, \(E_e\) its original exact and eligible support, \(A_c\) Ground Area, \(H^{\max}_{e,c}\) reference Peak Mean Depth and \(\widehat{H}^{\max}_{e,c}\) its prediction. Each training parent receives one shuffled full-field update per epoch. The fixed optimizer is AdamW with learning rate 0.001, weight decay 0.00001 and gradient norm limit 10. One seed and a maximum of forty epochs define the bounded trial. Validate after epoch one and every five epochs; choose the checkpoint minimizing parent-macro, Ground Area weighted absolute error on validation exact support. Stop after four validation checks without an improvement exceeding 0.000001 m. These settings are an implemented first baseline, without a hyperparameter search.

Report parent-macro depth MAE, RMSE, signed bias, reference-wet MAE, threshold overlap, precision, recall, missed area and false area. The primary wet threshold is strictly greater than 0.10 m, with 0.05, 0.30 and 0.50 m views retained. Undefined empty-denominator metrics remain not applicable, rather than perfect. Depth and extent metrics refer to common-cell mean peak exceedance, not simultaneous flooded area. Show domain and ward results and both paired and own-support coverage. Prepared-feature forward time is a limited compute diagnostic, not End-to-End Runtime or hydraulic speedup.

The fit stops after thirty-five epochs and 420 parent updates; the validation-selected checkpoint is epoch fifteen. The detailed validation outcome and its claim boundary are recorded in Section 7. No numerical tolerance, reference-quality mask or sample allocation is changed to improve the result.''')
 oldintro='The first four milestones establish input meaning, reference labels, scenario diversity and surrogate reliability. Current authorization is limited to the two open-control replays and their interface repairs; it does not extend to training or the prospective batch. Active measures remain Milestone 5. Methods remain planned; the minimum-library forcing generator, volume checks, lineage audit and forcing partitions are now implemented. The current update reports two separately authorized existing-control replays; training and the prospective batch remain unexecuted.'
 text=text.replace(oldintro,'The first four milestones establish input meaning, reference labels, scenario diversity and surrogate reliability. Current completed scope now includes the separately authorized sixteen-parent response tranche and one bounded exact-label conditional U-Net learning trial with two simple baselines. Earlier qualification paragraphs below are historical checkpoints. The remaining architecture and supervision comparisons, forty unrun hydraulic descendants, sealed tests and active-measure response library remain pending. Active measures remain Milestone 5.',1)
 u=mm['conditional_unet'];n=mm['retrieval'];dry=mm['dry']
 evidence=f'''### First-learning outcome and evidence boundary

The single first fit is complete under the original twelve-training/four-validation partition, exact masks and training-only normalization. On paired three-ward exact support, averaging the four validation parents, the conditional U-Net has MAE {u['mae_m']:.8f} m, reference-wet MAE {u['wet_mae_m']:.8f} m, and wet-extent intersection-over-union {u['iou_0.1']:.8f} at 0.10 m. The retrieval baseline gives MAE {n['mae_m']:.8f} m, reference-wet MAE {n['wet_mae_m']:.8f} m and intersection-over-union {n['iou_0.1']:.8f}. Always-dry gives MAE {dry['mae_m']:.8f} m and zero wet recall. The learned model does not improve either overall MAE or wet overlap over retrieval and does not improve overall MAE over always-dry. Its wet recall is {u['recall_0.1']:.8f}, so nearly all reference-wet area is missed in this trial. The small overall depth error must not be interpreted as successful preservation of accumulation areas.

| analytical step | variables used | model or specification | planned evidence connection | support status |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Preserve sample and reference custody | Rainfall Rate, River Stage, Peak Mean Depth, Ground Area | Original event and cell admission; trial-only exact access | Scenario coverage and split audit; Reference uncertainty | Technical custody checks pass; full-study outputs remain pending. |
| Fit one bounded peak emulator | Ground Elevation, Ground Area, Building Occupancy, Road Connectivity, Rainfall Rate, River Stage, Initial Water State, Surface Parameters, Peak Mean Depth | Exact-only conditional U-Net and area-weighted loss in Section 6 | Held-out surrogate performance; Held-out metric and runtime summary | Development fitting completed; independent held-out claim remains pending. |
| Compare cheap alternatives | Rainfall Rate, River Stage, Ground Area, Peak Mean Depth, Peak Wet Area | Always-dry and one-nearest training parent; identical paired exact support | Held-out surrogate performance; Held-out metric and runtime summary | This bounded U-Net recipe fails to retain the reference accumulation footprint or beat retrieval. |
| Preserve subsequent stages | Measure Configuration, Mitigation Benefit, Boundary Exchange | Later paired reference action/no-action comparison | Paired measure benefits and risk transfer; Physically checked measure comparison | Pending; no measure simulation or ranking evidence. |

All trial custody, support, normalization, prediction and metric checks pass. This is a negative development result for one small recipe and budget, not evidence that conditional U-Net or machine learning generally cannot emulate this reference. Low wet recall is observed; the roles of loss imbalance, optimization, model capacity and event diversity remain unisolated explanations. Diagnose these using development data before deciding a separately scoped improvement. Do not silently refit, enlarge the event library or expose sealed outcomes because this first fit underperforms. The planned Section 8 sealed-test and controlled-comparison figures and tables remain pending; the current exploratory report does not complete them.'''
 text=append_to(text,7,evidence)
 assert all(section(before,n)==section(text,n) for n in [1,2,8]);assert text.isascii();path.write_text(text)
 write(REPORT/'anasop_update.json',{'decision':'MILI-D-20261016-002','changed_sections':[3,4,5,6,7],'protected_sections_unchanged':[1,2,8],'responsibilities':{'3':'data-briefing','4':'data-preprocessing','5-7':'estimation-framework-planning'},'previous_sha256':sha(REPORT/'previous-AnaSOP.md'),'current_sha256':sha(path),'english_ascii_check':True,'published_outputs_marked_complete':False,'evidence':'Completed single fit, unchanged source hashes, event-level paired and own-support metrics, and delivery validation.'})
 print(json.dumps({'updated':[3,4,5,6,7],'protected':[1,2,8],'ascii':True}))
if __name__=='__main__':main()
